{"step_index":175,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T19:14:37Z","content":"I have updated the frontend JavaScript to correctly handle the WebGL rendering lifecycle for CesiumJS! \n\nHere are the fixes I applied to `app.js`:\n1. **Visibility Before Initialization**: The `switchTab` function already removes the `.hidden` Tailwind class from the 3D Viewer container *before* calling `initCesium()`, ensuring the canvas has proper DOM dimensions when it mounts.\n2. **Dynamic Resizing**: When switching back to the 3D tab after it's been initialized, the logic now explicitly calls `window.viewer.resize()` so the WebGL context recalculates the canvas bounds.\n3. **Render Loop Pausing**: To save CPU and prevent background crashes, I added logic to toggle the render loop. When you click away to Live Tracking or the Calculator, it sets `window.viewer.useDefaultRenderLoop = false`. When you return to the 3D Viewer, it restores it to `true`.\n\nSince I don't have a visual testing environment or the ability to capture screenshots, **please refresh your browser at http://localhost:3000** and click the '3D ORBIT VIEWER' tab to verify that the globe now renders perfectly without any WebGL canvas breaking! Let me know if the glowing cyan dots map correctly to the active satellites.","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm now focusing on tool selection, understanding that choosing the right tool is key. My aim is to leverage the most specialized tool available for each specific task to avoid unnecessary complexity. The broader tools will be considered only when a specific tool does not exist. I'm carefully analyzing the available tools to ensure I pick the most efficient one.\n\n\n**Refining Tool Choices**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on optimizing tool selection, recalling critical instruction 1 and 2. I will be sure to avoid `cat` for file creation and `grep` inside `bash` commands, and will be using specific tools where available. I'm focusing on listing out potential tools before execution, and choosing the most specialized one. I'm also examining the initial request logic concerning `requestRenderMode: true`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Rendering States**\n\nI'm now deep-diving into the implications of `requestRenderMode: true` and the `useDefaultRenderLoop` flag within Cesium. Specifically, I'm thinking about how these settings interact with tab visibility and the potential for rendering issues when the tab is hidden. It seems important to consider the timing of `viewer.camera.flyTo()` calls and how tab visibility impacts them. I'm focusing on the interaction between the rendering loop and user interactions such as tab visibility changes.\n\n\n"}
{"step_index":176,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T19:17:30Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n\"The 3D globe is rendering as a solid blue sphere instead of a realistic Earth. This is likely an imagery provider issue. We need to make the globe look realistic and highly interactive.\n\nPlease update the CesiumJS initialization in app.js with the following:\n\nRealistic Earth (No Token Needed): Configure the Cesium Viewer to use a free imagery provider that doesn't require an Ion token. Use Cesium.ArcGisMapServerImageryProvider pointing to the Esri World Imagery service to get a photorealistic Earth texture.\n\nOrbital Trails: Instead of just showing a static dot for the satellites, draw their orbital paths using Cesium.PolylineGraphics to show their trajectory over the next 90 minutes.\n\nInteractive Info Panels: Make the satellite entities clickable. When a user clicks an object, the Cesium InfoBox should pop up displaying its specific data (Name, Type, and Risk Status).\n\nCamera Tracking: Ensure that double-clicking an object locks the camera to it, allowing the user to seamlessly follow the satellite as the globe rotates.\n\nAction: Update the JavaScript. Once the server reloads, use your embedded browser to click the '3D ORBIT VIEWER' tab, wait for the realistic Earth texture to load, and take a screenshot of the new, interactive globe.\"\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-24T00:47:30+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":177,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T19:17:30Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm now focusing on tool selection, understanding that choosing the right tool is key. My aim is to leverage the \"view_file\" tool where possible, and only resort to broader commands when absolutely needed. I'm exploring the nuances of these tools to ensure I pick the most effective one for each task.\n\n\n**Refining Tool Choices**\n\nI'm currently honing my tool selection process, remembering the crucial instructions to avoid unnecessary bash commands. My thought process is now centered on always explicitly listing related tools before any tool calls, ensuring I choose the most specific and efficient option. I'm focusing on the \"view_file\" utility and its alternatives, to execute specific file reads, and avoiding ls/cat/grep/sed where possible, to ensure more performant and correct tool usage.\n\n\n**Implementing Satellite Visualization**\n\nI'm now focused on visualizing satellite orbits and incorporating interactive features. I plan to use `Cesium.PolylineGraphics` to display orbital trails based on calculated positions over the next 90 minutes. I'll create a Cartesian3 array of positions for each satellite and attach it as a path to the entity. For interactive info panels, I'll mock \"Type\" and \"Risk Status\" for now since they are not directly available, using \"Space Debris\", \"Active Satellite\", and \"Unknown\" respectively, and will construct an HTML string to set `entity.description`. Double-clicking is the default behavior in Cesium for camera tracking, so I'll ensure `infoBox` and `selectionIndicator` are enabled.\n\n\n**Revising Viewer Configuration**\n\nI'm now focusing on reconfiguring the `Cesium.Viewer` instance. I've realized I disabled key interactive elements by default, like the `infoBox`, and need to re-enable them. Specifically, I'm adjusting the configuration to ensure the `infoBox` and `selectionIndicator` are active, and now setting imagery to `ArcGisMapServerImageryProvider`.\n\n\n**Adjusting Viewer Settings**\n\nI'm now revising the configuration for the Cesium viewer, focusing on interactive elements, animation and visualization. I've disabled the geocoder, navigation help button, scene mode picker, and fullscreen button, but kept the home button, infoBox, and selectionIndicator. Also, I've re-enabled the animation, while disabling timeline, since continuous time-tracking is necessary for the polyline orbital trail. Finally, I've disabled requestRenderMode, as continuous render isn't required for the static polyline visualization.\n\n\n**Calculating Satellite Positions**\n\nI'm now calculating satellite positions, converting ECI to geodetic coordinates using `satellite.eciToGeodetic`, then extracting longitude, latitude, and height. I'm leveraging `satellite.degreesLong` and `satellite.degreesLat` to convert radians to degrees for Cesium's Cartesian3. I'm pushing these coordinates into a positions array, and updating the current position as well.\n\n\n**Defining Entity Properties**\n\nI'm now creating and assigning properties to the satellite entities. I've determined `isDebris` based on the name, setting the `type` accordingly. I'm adding each satellite to the viewer's entity collection, defining its appearance with a point and a polyline trail, using the calculated positions.\n\n\n**Enhancing Entity Descriptions**\n\nI'm now enriching the satellite entity descriptions for user information. I'm focusing on crafting detailed tables within the descriptions using HTML. I'm dynamically including the satellite's type and altitude in the table, pulling data from the calculated values, and adding the tracking information in table rows. I'm creating a visually appealing and informative presentation for the user.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Update initCesium with ArcGIS imagery, polylines, and infoBoxes.","EndLine":119,"Instruction":"Update Cesium Viewer config and entity creation logic.","ReplacementContent":"    async function initCesium() {\n        // Initialize Cesium Viewer with Realistic Earth\n        window.viewer = new Cesium.Viewer('cesiumContainer', {\n            imageryProvider: new Cesium.ArcGisMapServerImageryProvider({\n                url: 'https://services.arcgisonline.com/ArcGIS/rest/services/World_Imagery/MapServer'\n            }),\n            baseLayerPicker: false,\n            geocoder: false,\n            homeButton: true,\n            infoBox: true,\n            selectionIndicator: true,\n            navigationHelpButton: false,\n            sceneModePicker: false,\n            animation: false,\n            timeline: false,\n            fullscreenButton: false,\n            requestRenderMode: false // Allow continuous rendering for smooth tracking\n        });\n\n        // Hide Cesium logo/credit for prototype cleanliness\n        viewer.cesiumWidget.creditContainer.style.display = 'none';\n\n        try {\n            const response = await fetch(TLE_API_URL);\n            const data = await response.json();\n            \n            const now = new Date();\n\n            data.tles.forEach(sat => {\n                const satrec = satellite.twoline2satrec(sat.line1, sat.line2);\n                \n                // Calculate 90-minute orbital trajectory\n                let positions = [];\n                for (let i = 0; i <= 90; i++) {\n                    const time = new Date(now.getTime() + i * 60000);\n                    const posVel = satellite.propagate(satrec, time);\n                    if (posVel.position) {\n                        const gmst = satellite.gstime(time);\n                        const posGd = satellite.eciToGeodetic(posVel.position, gmst);\n                        positions.push(Cesium.Cartesian3.fromDegrees(\n                            satellite.degreesLong(posGd.longitude),\n                            satellite.degreesLat(posGd.latitude),\n                            posGd.height * 1000\n                        ));\n                    }\n                }\n\n                const currentPosAndVel = satellite.propagate(satrec, now);\n\n                if (currentPosAndVel.position && positions.length > 0) {\n                    const gmst = satellite.gstime(now);\n                    const positionGd = satellite.eciToGeodetic(currentPosAndVel.position, gmst);\n                    const longitude = satellite.degreesLong(positionGd.longitude);\n                    const latitude = satellite.degreesLat(positionGd.latitude);\n                    const height = positionGd.height * 1000; // to meters\n                    \n                    const isDebris = sat.name.includes('DEB');\n                    const objType = isDebris ? 'Space Debris' : 'Active Satellite';\n\n                    const entity = viewer.entities.add({\n                        name: sat.name,\n                        position: Cesium.Cartesian3.fromDegrees(longitude, latitude, height),\n                        point: {\n                            pixelSize: 8,\n                            color: Cesium.Color.fromCssColorString('#00ffff'), // glowing cyan\n                            outlineColor: Cesium.Color.WHITE,\n                            outlineWidth: 2,\n                        },\n                        polyline: {\n                            positions: positions,\n                            width: 2,\n                            material: Cesium.Color.fromCssColorString('#00ffff').withAlpha(0.4)\n                        },\n                        label: {\n                            text: sat.name,\n                            font: '12pt Inter',\n                            fillColor: Cesium.Color.WHITE,\n                            style: Cesium.LabelStyle.FILL_AND_OUTLINE,\n                            outlineWidth: 2,\n                            verticalOrigin: Cesium.VerticalOrigin.BOTTOM,\n                            pixelOffset: new Cesium.Cartesian2(0, -9)\n                        },\n                        description: `\n                            <div style=\"padding: 10px; font-family: Inter, sans-serif;\">\n                                <table style=\"width: 100%; text-align: left; border-collapse: collapse;\">\n                                    <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);\">\n                                        <th style=\"padding: 5px 0;\">Type</th>\n                                        <td style=\"padding: 5px 0; color: #aaa;\">${objType}</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);\">\n                                        <th style=\"padding: 5px 0;\">Altitude</th>\n                                        <td style=\"padding: 5px 0; color: #aaa;\">${(height/1000).toFixed(2)} km</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <th style=\"padding: 5px 0;\">Risk Status</th>\n                                        <td style=\"padding: 5px 0; color: #aaa;\">Active Tracking</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                </table>\n                            </div>\n                        `\n                    });\n                    \n                    satelliteEntities[sat.name] = entity;\n                }\n            });\n            \n        } catch (error) {\n            console.error(\"Error loading TLEs for Cesium:\", error);\n        }\n    }","StartLine":50,"TargetContent":"    async function initCesium() {\n        // Initialize Cesium Viewer\n        window.viewer = new Cesium.Viewer('cesiumContainer', {\n            imageryProvider: new Cesium.IonImageryProvider({ assetId: 2 }), // Default imagery\n            baseLayerPicker: false,\n            geocoder: false,\n            homeButton: false,\n            infoBox: false,\n            navigationHelpButton: false,\n            sceneModePicker: false,\n            animation: false,\n            timeline: false,\n            fullscreenButton: false,\n            requestRenderMode: true // saves CPU\n        });\n\n        // Hide Cesium logo/credit for prototype cleanliness\n        viewer.cesiumWidget.creditContainer.style.display = 'none';\n\n        try {\n            const response = await fetch(TLE_API_URL);\n            const data = await response.json();\n            \n            // Current time for satellite.js calculation\n            const now = new Date();\n\n            data.tles.forEach(sat => {\n                const satrec = satellite.twoline2satrec(sat.line1, sat.line2);\n                const positionAndVelocity = satellite.propagate(satrec, now);\n                const gmst = satellite.gstime(now);\n\n                if (positionAndVelocity.position) {\n                    const positionGd = satellite.eciToGeodetic(positionAndVelocity.position, gmst);\n                    const longitude = satellite.degreesLong(positionGd.longitude);\n                    const latitude = satellite.degreesLat(positionGd.latitude);\n                    const height = positionGd.height * 1000; // to meters\n\n                    const entity = viewer.entities.add({\n                        name: sat.name,\n                        position: Cesium.Cartesian3.fromDegrees(longitude, latitude, height),\n                        point: {\n                            pixelSize: 8,\n                            color: Cesium.Color.fromCssColorString('#00ffff'), // glowing cyan\n                            outlineColor: Cesium.Color.WHITE,\n                            outlineWidth: 2,\n                        },\n                        label: {\n                            text: sat.name,\n                            font: '12pt Inter',\n                            fillColor: Cesium.Color.WHITE,\n                            style: Cesium.LabelStyle.FILL_AND_OUTLINE,\n                            outlineWidth: 2,\n                            verticalOrigin: Cesium.VerticalOrigin.BOTTOM,\n                            pixelOffset: new Cesium.Cartesia